# M4 experiment: same as e2e-15.4-radiodiag.resc but with SetGlobalSerialExecution FALSE (true parallel
# cores). Hypothesis: parallel M33 + sequencer cores let the RAC Storage0 mailbox handshake complete
# concurrently (as on real silicon), curing the two-core livelock that wedges the radio post-operational.
# RISK: parallel cores were previously pinned OFF because they desynced the host-bridge (BLE/15.4) real-time
# timing -> commissioning may break earlier. This run tests empirically whether that still holds.
mach create "stock"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/silabs/brd2601b.repl
machine LoadPlatformDescription @matter/renode-thread/scenarios/phase3-bridges.repl
sysbus LoadELF @matter/brd2601b-matter-silabs-lighting-example.out
cpu PerformanceInMips 39
seqcpu PerformanceInMips 39
emulation CreateBLEMedium "wireless"
connector Connect sysbus.radio wireless
connector Connect sysbus.bleCentral wireless
connector Connect sysbus.ieee802154 wireless
emulation SetGlobalSerialExecution false
emulation SetGlobalAdvanceImmediately false
logFile @/tmp/renode-15.4.log true
logLevel 2
logLevel 1 sysbus.radio
logLevel 1 sysbus.ieee802154
start
